<BaseLayout lang="en" page="classes" title="Classes – Studio Sun & Sea">
  <h1>Classes</h1>

  <section id="foundational">
    <h2><a href="/en/schedule">Kunga Yoga Flow</a></h2>

    <p>
      Kunga Yoga Flow classes link breath and movement in creative sequences that work all of the major joints and muscles of the body and incorporate extended holds. This class is open to all levels and accessible to any and all body types. Posture (Āsana) alignment, meditation, breathing techniques (Prāṇāyāma), movement, and mindfulness are introduced. Use props to support your poses. Feel comfortable in the foundational postures that are offered.
    </p>

    <p>
      Kunga Yoga is a service-oriented non-lineage style of yoga for all people of all backgrounds, shapes, sizes, and abilities. „Kunga“ is a Rwandan word meaning „to help or to serve“. Please take personal responsibility for your safety and your needs, honoring your practice in the way that suits you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="yin-restorative">
    <h2>Yin / Restorative</h2>
    <p>
      A slow, grounding, deeply supportive practice.<br />
      If you’d like to see Yin on the weekly schedule, let us know — we add new classes based on community interest.Slow, grounding, and supportive practice.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="barre">
    <h2>Barre</h2>
    <p>
      Strength, alignment, rhythm, and mindful conditioning.<br />
      Barre classes can be added to the schedule when there is enough interest. Tell us if you’d join.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="meditation">
    <h2>Meditation</h2>
    <p>
      A quiet, guided space to settle, breathe, and reconnect.<br />
      Meditation sessions are offered when there is community demand. Share your interest anytime.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
